Third-party components and combined work
=======================================

BlockSec HookScan: https://github.com/blocksecteam/hookscan
  AGPL component invoked as an isolated process/container. No HookScan source is
  redistributed here; users obtain the engine separately. Attribution in reports
  remains intact.

Slither: https://github.com/crytic/slither
  AGPL-3.0-only. The detectors/ plugin links its internals. The independent CLI
  invokes analysis through external processes; source permissions remain separate.

Uniswap V4 Core/Periphery, OpenZeppelin, Forge Standard Library and Solmate:
  Retrieved at revisions in harness/deps.lock. Licenses differ by repository and
  source file, including MIT, Apache, BUSL, AGPL and UNLICENSED declarations.
  Some harness files import Solmate mocks and Uniswap test contracts; probes use
  the upstream Pool library. At the Solmate pin, imported MockERC20/ERC20 files
  declare MIT. The V4 Pool library declares BUSL, and upstream test routers and
  deployers declare UNLICENSED. Do not infer uniform MIT or an absent linkage
  from the old broad repository notice. The detector's Slither AGPL is separate.
  Custom notices on independently authored files do not relicense upstream source
  or compiled combined artifacts. Their redistribution/use requires the actual
  upstream rights and compatible terms. This policy change does not establish
  permission for a dependency whose upstream grant is missing or uncertain.

ajv: https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv
  MIT. The CLI runtime dependency retains its package license and attribution.

